s":[],"preserve":[],"line_breaks":true,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":2866,"kind":"presentation-binding"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.how_the_model_s_work_is_brought_back_up_when_it__62607e09","surface":"in_game","section":"dlssnr-menu","control":"tooltip","english":"How the model's work is brought back up when it ran below the frame's size.\n\nClassic composes the model's small picture directly against the full-size\nframe. Those two disagree by the shrink's blur as well as by the model's edit,\nand the composition cannot tell them apart -- it reads the blur as brightness\nthe frame has and the model never saw. The lower the model resolution the\nlarger that error, and it is the colour shift that shows up at 50%.\n\nMatched residual carries up only the model's difference and lays it on the\nframe's own proxy, so both pictures being compared are full size and the only\nthing that came from the small raster is the edit itself.\n\nNo effect at 100% or above: there is no residual to carry and the two are\nidentical (supersampling brings its answer down to frame size before this).\n\nFrom hhkbble's multi-pass work on this fork.","context":"Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","placeholders":[],"preserve":[],"line_breaks":true,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":1982,"kind":"presentation-binding"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.how_the_model_s_work_is_brought_back_up_when_it__7d541b42","surface":"in_game","section":"dlssnr-menu","control":"paragraph","english":"How the model's work is brought back up when it ran below the frame's size.","context":"Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","placeholders":[],"preserve":[],"line_breaks":false,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":2188,"kind":"provider"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.hybrid_composed_the_best_of_both_and_the_one_to__c8800358","surface":"in_game","section":"dlssnr-menu","control":"l