,"token":"%u"}],"preserve":[],"line_breaks":false,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":2281,"kind":"presentation-binding"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.what_it_cannot_show_dlss_fsr_xess_upscaler_prese_89ade1fe","surface":"in_game","section":"dlssnr-menu","control":"paragraph","english":"What it CANNOT show: DLSS/FSR/XeSS upscaler presets or anything upstream","context":"Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","placeholders":[],"preserve":["DLSS"],"line_breaks":false,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":3002,"kind":"provider"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.what_the_frame_is_divided_by_before_the_model_se_8020353d","surface":"in_game","section":"dlssnr-menu","control":"tooltip","english":"What the frame is divided by before the model sees it. There is no other white\npoint; this is the whole of it.\n\nThe model was trained on finished frames where white sits at 1. The\nupscaler's output is linear and open-ended, so something has to say where\nwhite is -- and where the game's DLSS buffer is linear HDR, that number is\nrarely anywhere near 1. Measured in Monster Hunter Wilds it takes 16 or more\nbefore the model's detail reaches the frame at all, and the value that suits\na shaded camp is still too small for the same game out in daylight.\n\nToo low and almost every pixel trips the soft knee: the model is shown a\nflat near-white picture, its answer is scaled away, and only its hue\nsurvives -- which reads as a colour cast rather than as lost detail. Too\nhigh and it is shown an underexposed one, its answer degrades, and this same\nnumber multiplies that error on the way out.\n\nRaise it until the picture stops improving. Past that point it does not\nplateau, it gets worse in the other direction.\n\nThis was once a multiplier on a measured white point. The measurement is\ngone: it read scene brightness rather than where white belongs, handed the\nmodel a picture three times too dark, and left the highlig)NR_ENGLISH",
R"NR_ENGLISH(ht path nothing to\ngive back.\n\nAt strength zero the frame is still bit-identical whatever this says.","context":"Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","placeholders":[],"preserve":["DLSS"],"line_breaks":true,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":2489,"kind":"presentation-binding"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.what_the_frame_is_divided_by_before_the_model_se_dd309029","surface":"in_game","section":"dlssnr-menu","control":"paragraph","english":"What the frame is divided by before the model sees it. There is no other white","context":"Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","placeholders":[],"preserve":[],"line_breaks":false,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":2695,"kind":"provider"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.what_the_model_is_shown_and_how_its_answer_comes_1ad8f03f","surface":"in_game","section":"dlssnr-menu","control":"tooltip","english":"What the model is shown, and how its answer comes back.\n\nOff (soft knee): the default. It rolls highlights off so hard the model\ncannot resolve detail in them -- fine in soft-lit scenes, weak in bright ones.\n\nNeutwo composed: an unclipped curve so the model sees highlight detail, then\neverything above (Detail/Colour strength, highlight guard, palette). It wins in\nbright scenes, but the curve compresses MIDTONES too, so in soft-lit content it\ncan be worse than Off. It also shifts paper white -- re-check it when you switch.\n\nHybrid composed: the best of both, and the one to use. Identity in the\nmidtones -- as good as Off there -- and the unclipped roll only in the\nhighlights, so it recovers the detail Off crushes without giving up the\nmidtones Neutwo does. It barely shifts paper white.\n\nReplace: the raw model straight back through the exact inverse, none of the\ncomposition -- no guard, no palette, no strengths. Gorgeous where there are no\nbright lights, but they FLASH in motion. A reference, not a daily setting.\n\nHybrid replace: the raw model like Replace, but on the hybrid curve -- the\ndecode is identity in the midtones, so the flashing is confined to genuine\nbright highlights instead of everywhere. Most of Replace's detail, far more\nstable. If you love the Replace look but the flicker bothers you, use this.\n\nOff is byte-identical to before.","context":"Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","placeholders":[],"preserve":[],"line_breaks":true,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":2012,"kind":"presentation-binding"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.what_the_model_is_shown_and_how_its_answer_comes_ff2d39f8","surface":"in_game","section":"dlssnr-menu","control":"label","english":"What the model is shown, and how its answer comes back.","context":"Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","placeholders":[],"preserve":[],"line_breaks":false,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":2218,"kind":"provider"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.where_the_number_that_divides_the_frame_comes_fr_2732b49d","surface":"in_game","section":"dlssnr-menu","control":"label","english":"Where the number that divides the frame comes from.","context":"Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","placeholders":[],"preserve":[],"line_breaks":false,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":2435,"kind":"provider"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.where_the_number_that_divides_the_frame_comes_fr_843c73a1","surface":"in_game","section":"dlssnr-menu","control":"tooltip","english":"Where the number that divides the frame comes from.\n\nPaper white only -- the slider below and nothing else. Right for a\ngame whose exposure never moves, wrong the moment it does: one\nconstant cannot serve a cave and a field.\n\nThe game's own exposure -- read from the texture the game hands\nthe upscaler. The best source there is, because it is decided\nupstream and nothing this pass does can move it. Not every game\nsupplies one.\n\nA buffer the scan found -- for games that compute an exposure and\nnever pass it on. A GUESS: candidates are matched by shape, and in\nGTA V the best one tracks the real exposure but at its own scale,\nwhich the anchor's ratio cancels. Needs anchoring once, and checking\nafterwards.","context":"Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","placeholders":[],"preserve":[],"line_breaks":true,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":2229,"kind":"presentation-binding"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.where_the_wipe_cuts_left_of_it_is_the_frame_as_t_0d17f9f5","surface":"in_game","section":"dlssnr-menu","control":"tooltip","english":"Where the wipe cuts. Left of it is the frame as the upscaler produced it,\nright of it is the frame the model edited.","context":"Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","placeholders":[],"preserve":[],"line_breaks":true,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":2882,"kind":"presentation-binding"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.where_the_wipe_cuts_left_of_it_is_the_frame_as_t_e857f27e","surface":"in_game","section":"dlssnr-menu","control":"paragraph","english":"Where the wipe cuts. Left of it is the frame as the upscaler produced it,","context":"Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","placeholders":[],"preserve":[],"line_breaks":false,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":3088,"kind":"provider"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.which_the_anchor_s_ratio_cancels_needs_anchoring_f92456a9","surface":"in_game","section":"dlssnr-menu","control":"label","english":"which the anchor's ratio cancels. Needs anchoring once, and checking","context":"Current UI: OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","placeholders":[],"preserve":[],"line_breaks":false,"revision":1,"sources":[{"path":"OptiScaler/dlssnr/DlssNr_Menu.cpp","line":2446,"kind":"provider"}]},{"id":"ingame.dlssnr-menu.white_is_and_where_the_game_s_dlss_buffer_is_lin_11994866","